  "body": "The browser build of `main` compiles again: the link check from #2463 now reads CamCraft's clock seam (`camcraft_app::clock::Instant`) instead of `std::time::Instant`, which is a different type on wasm32.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/ui/src/model_link_watch.rs`: `use camcraft_app::clock::Instant;` in place of `std::time::Instant`. Native builds get the same std type through the seam (#31), so nothing changes there; on wasm32 the seam is `web_time::Instant`, the type `State` already passes at `state.rs:3130`.\n\n## Readings\n\nmacOS, Homebrew clang 23 for wasm32 (`CC_wasm32_unknown_unknown` / `AR_wasm32_unknown_unknown` as in `release.yml`), built as a separate user with no credentials:\n- Before (on `main` at 409c0b5ab, via #2706's branch): `bash web/build-app-wasm.sh` fails with E0308 at `state.rs:3130` (#2708).\n- After: `bash web/build-app-wasm.sh` exit 0; `bash web/check-app-page.sh target/web`: \"4 files present; every URL relative to the page's folder; no SharedArrayBuffer\". `Cargo.lock` left untouched.\n- Also with #2706 merged on top: `web/build-app-wasm.sh` exit 0.\n- Native: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean; `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib model_link`: 3 passed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No new test: PR checks do not build wasm32, so a test here would not run there. The release job's `wasm` step is the check.\n- The page was built, not opened in a browser.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\nFork synced at v0.24.0 (branch from upstream main 409c0b5ab).\n\nFixes #2708\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd\n",
